{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Everything that comes into fire.</b> To cook in it anything." "<b>You shall pass through fire.</b> According to the manner of its use is its purging — one whose use is by means of hot liquid, purge it in hot liquid; and one whose use is by means of roasting, such as the spit and the grill, heat it white-hot in the fire (Avodah Zarah 74)." "<b>However, with the water of a menstruating woman it shall be cleansed.</b> According to its plain sense, this cleansing is to purify it from corpse impurity — He told them: the vessels require purging to purify them from the prohibition, and cleansing to purify them from the impurity. And our Sages derived from here that even to prepare them from the prohibition immersion was required for metal vessels, and 'the water of a menstruating woman' written here they interpreted as water fit for a menstruating woman to immerse in, and how much is it? Forty se'ah (there 75)." "<b>And everything that does not come into fire.</b> Any thing whose use is not by means of fire, such as cups and bowls whose use is for cooling, and they did not absorb the prohibition." "<b>You shall pass through water.</b> Immerse them, and that suffices — and specifically metal vessels."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:29.612029257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}